                  "text": "There are two good things about running experiments in Graphwell.<br><br>The first is that there are plenty to choose from. There are <a href=\"https://example.com\" style=\"color:#E8742C\">A/B tests</a>, of course, but also <a href=\"https://example.com\" style=\"color:#E8742C\">multivariate tests</a>, <a href=\"https://example.com\" style=\"color:#E8742C\">holdout groups</a> and <a href=\"https://example.com\" style=\"color:#E8742C\">redirect tests</a>.<br><br>The <em>other</em> good thing is that once you’ve set one up, you can get on with something else while the numbers come in. We call that delegating.",
